PUBLIC RESPONSE: Essay: *El escritor argentino y la tradición* / “The Argentine Writer and the Tradition”, *Discusión* 1932, reprinted in *Otras indagaciones / Other Inquisitions*. 

In the paragraph on *las ilusiones del patriotismo no tienen fin / the illusions of patriotism have no end* Borges gives the classic national-panegyric triad of a Greek, an Englishman and a German:

* the Greek historian Herodotus, the Hellenic “measure of civilisation” topos;
* the English poet John Milton, who writes that God revealed Himself first in English;
* the German philosopher Johann Gottlieb Fichte, who calls the German people the chosen people in the *Addresses to the German Nation*.

Herodotus, Milton, Fichte

