10.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The deliberation has converged strongly on Locus A for the exact wording “las ilusiones del patriotismo no tienen fin / the illusions of patriotism have no end”. The sentence is the patriotic-illusion nucleus first drafted as *Patriotismo* 1926-27 and rewritten for *Discusión* 1932 as *El escritor argentino y la tradición*, anthologised in *Otras indagaciones / Other Inquisitions* as *Patria / The Argentine Nation / The Argentine Writer and the Tradition*.

Locus A triad is now stable across colleagues 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,10,11,12,13,14 in round 4:
* Greek – Herodotus, pan-Hellenic “Greeks are the best people in the world” encomium;
* Englishman – John Milton, *Areopagitica*, God reveals himself first in English / England as a chosen noble and puissant nation;
* German – Johann Gottlieb Fichte, *Reden an die deutsche Nation*, German people as chosen people.

Evidence supporting Locus A: the wording is the opening of the patriotic-illusion paragraph in the *Discusión / Other Inquisitions* form, and Milton is invariant across all reconstructions. The Plutarch–Milton–Hegel triad is now characterized as the neighbouring *El pudor de la historia / The Modesty of History* material, or as a conflation/paraphrase mix-up. Colleagues explicitly reject the hybrid Plutarch–Milton–Fichte as mixing Greek from the Modesty of History line with English/German from the patriotic-illusion line.

Edition variants noted and retained as background noise:
* Herodotus – Samuel Johnson – Johann Gottfried Herder variant in some *Patria* printings;
* earlier spurious suggestions Pindar/Macaulay/Heine, Pericles/Wagner, Plutarch/Shakespeare/Fichte, etc., now treated as spurious or contamination.

My current best reading remains Locus A, with essay *El escritor argentino y la tradición / Patria* and names Herodotus, Milton, Fichte. Title wording *El escritor argentino y la tradición* vs *Patria* reprint heading persists only nominally; the triad is stable. The Plutarch, Milton, Hegel alternative is understood as a distinct locus and contamination source, not the text for the quoted sentence. Unresolved nominal issue is only the precise essay heading; the triad attachment to the quoted sentence is settled.

